  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Second prerelease: the library's public API, settled for a 1.0. It breaks code written against 0.1.0-alpha. The engine's internals (the script engine, actors, sound players, decoders, renderers, resource index, save serializer) are no longer public. GameWorld is the way to play headless: boot, step, screen, input, saves and loads, and new CopyProtection, Audio, SkipCutscene, Variables and SetVariable, CurrentScript, RunningScripts and ActorsHere. GameInspector (Maniacal.Scumm.Inspection) is new: room pictures with their objects, costumes' figures, scripts decoded, and a room's screen with figures standing in it. Every public member is documented. The maniacal tool plays as before; its --room, --costume, --script and --view are built on the inspection API. Built and tested on Windows, Linux and macOS.",
